1. WHAT IS ORM (OBJECT RELATIONAL MAPPING)?
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Definition

    ORM is a technique that maps Java Objects to
    Database Tables automatically.

Mapping

    Java Class
        ↓
    Database Table

    Java Object
        ↓
    Database Row

    Java Variable
        ↓
    Database Column

    Java Relationship
        ↓
    Foreign Key

Example

    public class Account {

        private Long id;
        private BigDecimal balance;
    }

Table

    ACCOUNT

    ID      BALANCE
    1       1000

Without ORM

    Connection con =
            DriverManager.getConnection(...);

    PreparedStatement ps =
            con.prepareStatement(
            "select * from account"
            );

Lots of JDBC code.

With ORM

    Account account =
        accountRepository.findById(1L)
                         .orElseThrow();

Hibernate generates SQL automatically.

Advantages

    • Less Code
    • Better Maintainability
    • Object Oriented Programming
    • Automatic Relationship Handling
    • DB Independence

Banking Example

    Account
         ↓
    Transaction
         ↓
    Customer

All mapped as Java Objects.

Interview Question

    Why ORM?

Answer

    Eliminates repetitive JDBC code and
    improves productivity.

