27. persist() vs merge()
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

persist()

Purpose:

    Save New Entity

Example:

    Account account =
            new Account();

    entityManager.persist(account);

Result:

    Object becomes MANAGED.

-------------------------------------------------------

merge()

Purpose:

    Re-attach Detached Entity

Example:

    Account merged =
            entityManager.merge(account);

Important

    merge() returns Managed Copy.

Wrong

    entityManager.merge(account);

    account.setStatus(ACTIVE);

Correct

    Account merged =
        entityManager.merge(account);

    merged.setStatus(ACTIVE);

Interview Question

    When use persist()?

Answer

    New Entity

Interview Question

    When use merge()?

Answer

    Detached Entity

