29. WHAT IS DIRTY CHECKING?
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Definition

    Hibernate automatically detects changes
    to Managed Entities.

Example

    @Transactional

    public void blockAccount(Long id){

        Account account =
            repository.findById(id)
                      .orElseThrow();

        account.setStatus(BLOCKED);
    }

Notice

    No save() required.

At Commit Time

Hibernate Generates

    UPDATE ACCOUNT
       SET STATUS='BLOCKED'
     WHERE ID=1

Interview Question

    Why no save()?

Answer

    Dirty Checking

Benefits

    Less Code

    Better Readability

